From e7f1d69ac795fe0ada01464d1ac5412ed303029e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: storm-factory <storm-factory@localhost>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 05:19:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] feat(frontend): translate inline assembly create2

The frontend translates the one inline assembly block
`target := create2(value, add(code, 32), mload(code), salt)` over
Solidity locals to the new statement `Stmt.assemblyCreate2`, which the
type checker accepts for an address target, a bytes memory init code,
and a literal or uint256 value and a literal, uint256 or bytes32 salt,
outside view and pure functions. It lowers to the core expression
`create2Bytes`, one open-world CREATE2 request whose init code is the
bytes of `code`: the address it answers, 0 on failure, without a
revert. Every other inline assembly block stays out of the fragment.

UniswapV2Factory is now translated whole, createPair included, and its
contract_ok holds. Contracts/Create2 tests the translation and the run
on a small contract, with frontend and type check negatives, and
Contracts/UniswapV2/Factory/Create2Run.lean runs createPair.
